---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="Community">
  <h1>Community</h1>
  <p>
    Outside the lab, I spend a lot of my time on mentoring and community
    work, and it's just as much a part of who I am as the science is.
  </p>

  <div class="card">
    <h3>Food Not Bombs East Bay</h3>
    <p class="pub-meta">Volunteer &middot; September 2024 &ndash; Present</p>
    <p>
      Every week, I pick up meals made by our team of volunteer cooks and
      serve 25 to 40 free vegetarian meals to unhoused and low-income
      neighbors. When I started, food for our shift was being dropped off in
      bags at the corner, so I began bringing a table and serving each meal
      in person, the way the other days' serves do. It's become one of the
      most grounding parts of my week, and a direct way to put my belief in
      mutual aid into practice.
    </p>
    <a
      class="btn secondary"
      href="https://eastbayfoodnotbombs.org/"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener noreferrer"
    >
      Visit East Bay Food Not Bombs
    </a>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h3>Sigma Xi, the Scientific Research Honor Society</h3>

    <p style="font-weight: 700; color: var(--pink-700); margin-bottom: 0.1rem;">
      Berkeley Chapter
    </p>
    <p style="font-weight: 600; color: var(--pink-500); margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0.2rem;">
      Vice President &amp; Committee for Student Advancement Chair
    </p>
    <p class="pub-meta">Associate Member &middot; September 2021 &ndash; Present</p>
    <p>
      As Vice President of the Berkeley chapter, I help run our semi-annual
      Grants in Aid of Research program, which awards research grants of up
      to $750 to undergraduate, master's, and PhD students across STEM, and
      I've led outreach to campus organizations and departments to grow the
      chapter. I founded the Committee for Student Advancement (CSA) to open
      Sigma Xi up to students who aren't yet eligible for membership,
      growing it to as many as 40 students and
      hosting networking events and student and guest talks, including
      a talk by the Editor-in-Chief of <em>American Scientist</em>. My
      biggest project was planning the Sigma Xi&ndash;ATP Bio Research
      Symposium &amp; Poster Session from scratch, from securing funding to
      coordinating the day itself, which brought together about 25 student
      presenters, a keynote speaker, and about 150 attendees who voted for a
      best-poster prize.
    </p>
    <a
      class="btn secondary"
      href="https://community.sigmaxi.org/communities/allcommunities/chaptergroupdetails?CommunityKey=4d4241bc-8689-4e5f-839e-f9edcd89c314"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener noreferrer"
    >
      Visit Berkeley Chapter of SX
    </a>

    <p style="font-weight: 700; color: var(--pink-700); margin-top: 1.75rem; margin-bottom: 0.1rem; padding-top: 1.5rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line);">
      Northeastern University Chapter
    </p>
    <p style="font-weight: 600; color: var(--pink-500); margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0.2rem;">
      Diversity &amp; Inclusion Chair
    </p>
    <p class="pub-meta">Associate Member &middot; July 2020 &ndash; May 2021</p>
    <p>
      As Diversity &amp; Inclusion Chair, I reached out to first-generation,
      culture-specific, and other underrepresented student groups to bring
      more students into Sigma Xi, and hosted a diversity, equity, and
      inclusion panel open to the whole campus.
    </p>
    <a
      class="btn secondary"
      href="https://sigmaxinortheastern.sites.northeastern.edu/"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener noreferrer"
    >
      Visit Northeastern Chapter of SX
    </a>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h3>Bay Area Bioscience Education Health &amp; Science Challenge (BioEHSC)</h3>
    <p class="pub-meta">Academic Judge &middot; April 2022 &ndash; April 2026</p>
    <p>
      Each spring, I volunteer as an academic judge for the Bay Area
      Bioscience Education Health &amp; Science Challenge (BioEHSC), a
      full-day pitch competition for high school teams. Paired with one
      or two other judges, who are PhDs, PhD students, or other STEM
      professionals, I watch 10 to 15 ten-minute team pitches
      followed by Q&amp;A, assessing each team's depth of knowledge and
      offering feedback where I can. It's one of my favorite volunteer
      days of the year, because I get to network with other judges and
      professionals, and watch high schoolers challenge themselves and
      come up with genuinely creative ideas.
    </p>
    <a
      class="btn secondary"
      href="https://bioehs.studentorg.berkeley.edu/bioehsc/"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener noreferrer"
    >
      Visit BioEHSC
    </a>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h3>Adventure Challenge</h3>
    <p class="pub-meta">Volunteer &middot; September 2018 &ndash; December 2019</p>
    <p>
      I was paired with a teen with autism through the
      Adventure Challenge program, planning weekly trips to the YMCA pool
      for swimming and pool games. The goal was simple but meaningful, to
      promote physical activity, social interaction, and overall health and
      wellness to help her stay healthy and active.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h3>Advancement Via Individual Determination (AVID)</h3>
    <p class="pub-meta">Tutor &middot; September 2018 &ndash; December 2018</p>
    <p>
      At Fenway High School in Boston, I led a weekly group of 6 to 8
      students in AVID, a program that prepares students from
      underrepresented and low-income backgrounds for college. Rather than
      handing out answers, I taught students to help each other work through
      challenging math and science problems by asking good questions and
      thinking critically. Hearing students worry about whether a school
      like Northeastern, just a five-minute walk away, was within reach
      made me want to break down those barriers to STEM.
    </p>
    <a
      class="btn secondary"
      href="https://www.avid.org/"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener noreferrer"
    >
      Visit AVID
    </a>
  </div>
  <div class="card">
    <h3>Northeastern University Club Triathlon</h3>
    <p class="pub-meta">September 2016 &ndash; June 2021</p>
    <p>
      I served as President and Captain (2019&ndash;2020), Chief Financial
      Officer (2018&ndash;2019), and Chief Procurement Officer
      (2017&ndash;2018), and represented club teams on the Club Sports
      Council (2019&ndash;2021).
    </p>
  </div>
</Layout>
